<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Chickadee brand strings. Overrides main/ for the chickadee* flavors only.

  ONE definition of the product name — do not scatter it. Every user-facing sentence that
  names the product should take this as a FORMAT ARGUMENT rather than being duplicated here;
  a per-source-set copy of a sentence drifts the moment the copy is edited on one side, and
  the compiler cannot see it. Same reasoning as `colors.xml` redirecting `orange` instead of
  copying five theme files.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="brand_name">Chickadee</string>

    <!--
      Product decision 2026-08-21: the chickadee domain registration was dropped, so the
      brand-specific screensaver URL override (previously the chickadee-domain parity page with
      `?weather=1`, per the 2026-08-02 prefill ruling) was removed rather than left pointing at a
      dead host. Chickadee flavors now inherit main/'s default_screensaver_url.

      ⚠️ That is NOT behavioural parity with the old override, and an earlier version of this
      comment claimed it was. Corrected 2026-08-22 after measuring the page:
        - main/'s URL is https://dashieapp.com/screensaver, with NO query parameter.
        - That page calls loadWeather() unconditionally on DOMContentLoaded and again every
          600 s, and loadWeather() fetches https://ipapi.co/json/ (the household's public IP to
          a third party) before open-meteo.
        - The page has NO query-parameter handling at all, so the old `?weather=1` was inert on
          it. The 2026-08-02 design — weather OFF by default, opted in per-device by that
          parameter — has no implementation here.
      So a device on this flavor that selects the URL mode gets an unconditional IP lookup on a
      10-minute timer. Long-standing behaviour for the Dashie brand and a known disclosure item;
      newly inherited here. Whether this flavor wants its own weather-off page is deferred while
      the brand is frozen — do not read this comment as saying the question was settled.

      The URL is only the PREFILL for an OPT-IN mode: the default screensaver MODE stays "dim"
      in both editions, so a household that never picks the URL mode never loads it.
    -->

</resources>
